Lab 3: Use RHACM Web Console to Inspect Resources Across Clusters
Lab Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

• Access and navigate the Red Hat Advanced Cluster Management (RHACM) Web Console • Search for and inspect resources such as pods, services, and deployments across multiple clusters • Drill down into cluster-specific details and configurations • Apply updates and modifications to resources through the web interface • Understand the centralized management capabilities of RHACM for multi-cluster environments

Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, you should have:

• Basic understanding of Kubernetes concepts (pods, services, deployments) • Familiarity with OpenShift Container Platform fundamentals • Knowledge of YAML configuration files • Basic understanding of container orchestration concepts • Completion of previous RHACM labs or equivalent experience

Required Knowledge Areas
• Kubernetes Resources: Understanding of core Kubernetes objects • OpenShift Concepts: Familiarity with OpenShift-specific resources • Web Browser Navigation: Comfortable using web-based interfaces • Command Line Basics: Basic terminal/command prompt usage

