Task 1: Access the RHACM Web Console
Subtask 1.1: Initial Console Access
Open your web browser and navigate to the RHACM console URL provided in your lab environment

Log in using the provided credentials:

Username: admin
Password: [provided in lab environment]
Verify successful login by confirming you see the RHACM dashboard with cluster overview

Subtask 1.2: Navigate the Console Interface
Explore the main navigation menu on the left side of the console

Identify key sections: • Clusters: View and manage all connected clusters • Applications: Manage multi-cluster applications • Governance: Policy and compliance management • Infrastructure: Cluster lifecycle management

Access the Overview dashboard to see cluster health status and resource summaries

Subtask 1.3: Verify Cluster Connectivity
Click on "Clusters" in the left navigation menu

Review the cluster list and verify you can see: • Hub cluster (local-cluster) • At least 2-3 managed clusters • Status indicators showing "Ready" for all clusters

Note cluster details such as: • Cluster names • OpenShift versions • Node counts • Status indicators

Task 2: Search for and Inspect Resources Across Clusters
Subtask 2.1: Use the Global Search Feature
Access the Search functionality: • Click on the search icon (magnifying glass) in the top navigation bar • Or navigate to Search from the main menu

Perform a basic resource search:

Search Query: kind:pod
Review search results showing pods from all managed clusters

Filter results by cluster: • Use the cluster filter dropdown • Select a specific cluster to narrow results

Subtask 2.2: Search for Specific Resource Types
Search for services across all clusters:

Search Query: kind:service
Search for deployments:

Search Query: kind:deployment
Search for resources in specific namespaces:

Search Query: kind:pod namespace:default
Use advanced search filters: • Label selectors: label:app=nginx • Resource status: kind:pod status:Running • Cluster-specific: cluster:managed-cluster-1 kind:service

Subtask 2.3: Inspect Pod Resources
Search for all pods:

Search Query: kind:pod
Select a pod from the results by clicking on its name

Review pod details: • Basic Information: Name, namespace, cluster location • Status: Current phase, restart count, age • Specifications: Container images, resource requests/limits • Events: Recent pod events and status changes

Navigate to pod logs: • Click on the Logs tab • Review container output and error messages • Use log filtering options if available

Subtask 2.4: Inspect Service Resources
Search for services:

Search Query: kind:service
Select a service from the search results

Examine service configuration: • Endpoints: Target pods and IP addresses • Ports: Service port mappings • Selectors: Pod selection criteria • Type: ClusterIP, NodePort, LoadBalancer, etc.

View related resources: • Click on Related Resources to see connected pods • Review endpoint configurations

Subtask 2.5: Inspect Deployment Resources
Search for deployments:

Search Query: kind:deployment
Select a deployment to view details

Review deployment specifications: • Replica count: Desired vs. current replicas • Update strategy: Rolling update configuration • Pod template: Container specifications • Conditions: Deployment status and health

Check deployment history: • Look for revision information • Review rollout status

Task 3: Drill Down into Cluster Specifics and Apply Updates
Subtask 3.1: Access Cluster-Specific Views
Navigate to the Clusters section

Select a specific managed cluster by clicking on its name

Explore cluster details: • Overview: Cluster health, resource usage, alerts • Nodes: Worker node status and specifications • Machine pools: Node group configurations • Add-ons: Installed cluster add-ons and operators

Review cluster metrics: • CPU and memory utilization • Storage usage • Network statistics

Subtask 3.2: Navigate to Cluster Resources
From the cluster details page, click on View cluster

Access the OpenShift console for the selected cluster

Navigate between RHACM and cluster-specific views: • Use browser tabs to maintain both interfaces • Note the different perspectives available

Subtask 3.3: Apply Resource Updates Through RHACM
Return to the RHACM console

Search for a deployment to modify:

Search Query: kind:deployment name:sample-app
Select the deployment and click Edit

Modify the replica count:

spec:
  replicas: 3  # Change from current value
Apply the changes: • Click Save or Apply • Confirm the update in the confirmation dialog

Verify the update: • Wait for the deployment to scale • Check that new pods are created • Confirm the replica count matches your change

Subtask 3.4: Update Resource Labels
Search for a service to modify:

Search Query: kind:service namespace:default
Select a service and access the Edit option

Add or modify labels:

metadata:
  labels:
    environment: production
    managed-by: rhacm
Save the changes and verify the labels are applied

Subtask 3.5: Monitor Update Progress
Use the search function to monitor your changes:

Search Query: kind:deployment name:sample-app
Check deployment status: • Verify replica count changes • Monitor pod creation/termination • Review deployment conditions

View events related to your changes: • Look for scaling events • Check for any error messages • Confirm successful updates

Task 4: Advanced Resource Management
Subtask 4.1: Cross-Cluster Resource Comparison
Search for the same application across multiple clusters:

Search Query: kind:deployment label:app=sample-app
Compare configurations between clusters: • Note differences in replica counts • Compare resource limits and requests • Identify configuration variations

Document differences for standardization purposes

Subtask 4.2: Bulk Resource Operations
Select multiple resources using the search interface: • Use checkboxes to select multiple pods or services • Apply filters to narrow selection

Perform bulk actions (if available): • Label multiple resources simultaneously • Apply common annotations • Perform bulk deletions (with caution)

Subtask 4.3: Resource Relationship Mapping
Select a deployment from search results

Explore resource relationships: • View associated ReplicaSets • Check connected Services • Identify related ConfigMaps or Secrets

Create a mental map of resource dependencies

Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: Console Access Problems
Symptoms: Cannot access RHACM web console Solutions: • Verify the correct URL is being used • Check network connectivity • Clear browser cache and cookies • Try a different browser or incognito mode

Issue 2: Search Results Not Appearing
Symptoms: Search queries return no results Solutions: • Verify cluster connectivity in the Clusters section • Check search syntax and filters • Ensure resources exist in the target clusters • Wait for search index to update (may take a few minutes)

Issue 3: Resource Updates Not Applied
Symptoms: Changes made through console don't take effect Solutions: • Verify you have appropriate permissions • Check for validation errors in the YAML • Ensure the target cluster is accessible • Review cluster events for error messages

Issue 4: Performance Issues
Symptoms: Console is slow or unresponsive Solutions: • Reduce the scope of search queries • Use specific filters to limit results • Check network latency to clusters • Consider browser resource usage

